   "outcomes": [
    "Apply theories and knowledge produced by Asian and Pacific Islander communities to interrogate and dismantle interlocking systems of oppression and dominant power structures.",
    "Develop a critical understanding of the intersectional histories and cultures of Asian and Pacific Islander communities as they relate to larger social structures to cultivate solidarity and coalitions across lines of difference.",
    "Examine and actively engage with anti-colonial, decolonial, liberatory, and radical resistance strategies, practices, and movements within Asian and Pacific Islander communities to advocate for the empowerment and liberation of minoritized and marginalized communities of color.",
    "Interrogate media and cultural productions by describing ways they construct dominant narratives and controlling images that affect the lived experiences of Asian and Pacific Islander communities",
    "Demonstrate an understanding of critical race and media literacy strategies by producing counter-narratives of Asian and Pacific Islander communities that contest existing oppressive experiences, stereotypes, and social norms within society."
